  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Also called plage du Port, Plage Vespins is lined with umbrella pines, supervised in summer and open to swimming for humans and dogs alike, according to the Nice Côte d'Azur tourist office. A large car park, the harbour's, is nearby.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The tourist office states that dogs are allowed on the whole beach, off-leash, but must swim in a clearly marked area delimited by two posts at the end of the beach. We found no municipal order that requires or rules out a leash: to be safe, keep your dog under control, pick up after it and stay responsible for its behaviour.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: this is one of the few beaches in the Nice area where dog swimming is explicitly provided for year-round.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Saint-Laurent-du-Var harbour and its waterfront restaurants are right next door, handy for extending the outing.</p>
    </div>

